=E6=82=A8=E5=A5=BD!

Lojban numbers are represented with the positional notation=20
<http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Positional_notation>: in base ten, the ten=20
primary digits {no, pa, re, ci, vo, mu, xa, ze, bi, so} (=3D 0, 1, 2, 3,=20
4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9) are enough for encoding any positive integer: 10 is=20
{pa no}, 100 is {pa no no}, 1000 is {pa no no no}, and so on. As a=20
result, there is no need for number words such as "hundred", "thousand",=20
"billions" etc.

In Lojban, =E4=B8=87 is expressed as {pa no no no no}, or {pa se gei vo}=20
(1=C3=9710^4, scientific notation).

It is also possible to specify the number base/radix by using the=20
particle {ju'u}, which allows for example to express numbers in base=20
two, base twelve, base sixteen etc.

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o

